Discussion:
The Safety/Security category has 29 atomic fields and 2 compounds
(TpmsHardWarnings, TpmsSoftWarnings). Both compounds carry a
protomodel.TireLocation value, which the codec expands into 10
boolean atomics each via flattenTireLocation in
internal/tesla/codec/flatten.go: the four passenger-car corners
(Front/Rear x Left/Right) plus six Semi-truck positions
(SemiMiddleAxleLeft2, SemiMiddleAxleRight2, SemiRearAxleLeft,
SemiRearAxleLeft2, SemiRearAxleRight, SemiRearAxleRight2). The
"_2" suffix on the second-axle Semi entries preserves the upstream
proto's Get*_2 accessor naming so a future operator cross-
referencing signal_log against the Tesla schema can find the
fields without renames. This prompt registers the codec-emitted
flatten names verbatim, not aliased simpler names, matching the
DoorState precedent set in prompt 0045.

Routing decisions (29 atomics):
  * 4 TpmsPressure{Fl,Fr,Rl,Rr} route to tire_pressure_snapshot
    columns front_left_pa / front_right_pa / rear_left_pa /
    rear_right_pa. UnitKindPressure triggers normalize.toSI
    conversion to Pascals via the Setting*Unit / vehicle_unit_history
    layer; the SI value lands in the snapshot.
  * 4 TpmsLastSeenPressureTime{Fl,Fr,Rl,Rr} route to
    tire_pressure_snapshot columns
    {front,rear}_{left,right}_last_seen_at. UnitKindNone so
    normalize.toSI is a pass-through; the writer converts the
    unix-epoch float to TIMESTAMPTZ.
  * Locked routes to security_event. Every lock/unlock transition
    is a discrete security-relevant event; the writer diffs against
    the previous observation and emits one row per transition.
  * 8 SemitruckTpmsPressureRe{1,2}{L,R}{0,1} (Semi six-axle TPMS,
    string-typed) route to signal_log. tire_pressure_snapshots
    models only the four passenger-car corners; the Semi tractor's
    dual-rear-axle layout has no hot column. The values are
    string-typed on the wire, so units conversion does not apply -
    the raw string is preserved.
  * 2 SemitruckTractorParkBrakeStatus + SemitruckTrailerParkBrakeStatus
    route to signal_log (Semi-specific brake split, no hot column).
  * 2 MilesSinceReset + SelfDrivingMilesSinceReset
    (UnitKindDistance) route to signal_log. normalize.toSI converts
    the wire value (km or mi depending on SettingDistanceUnit) to
    meters; the SI value lands in signal_log. Despite the legacy
    "Miles" name the wire value is in the active SettingDistanceUnit.
  * 9 driver-assist toggles route to signal_log:
    AutomaticBlindSpotCamera, AutomaticEmergencyBrakingOff,
    BlindSpotCollisionWarningChime, CruiseFollowDistance,
    EmergencyLaneDepartureAvoidance, ForwardCollisionWarning,
    LaneDepartureAvoidance, PinToDriveEnabled. These are
    configuration-shaped flags / sensitivity ordinals; the
    safety_snapshots hot table tracks service / wiper / crash
    flags, not the per-feature ADAS toggles.
  * 20 Tpms{Hard,Soft}Warnings flatten atomics route to signal_log.
    tire_pressure_snapshots.{hard,soft}_warnings is a single TEXT
    token aggregating the per-corner bits; the snapshot writer
    reads the per-corner change stream from signal_log to populate
    the per-corner *_status columns and the rolled-up warning
    tokens, rather than the router dispatching directly to the
    snapshot table for each corner. Same precedent as DoorState
    in prompt 0045.

Notes on the prompt's example list:
  * SentryMode / ValetMode / SpeedLimitMode / SpeedLimitWarning /
    GuestModeMobileAccessState / ServiceMode are vehicle_state
    category, NOT safety_security; they were routed by prompt 0045.
    The prompt's text uses them as examples of the routing rule
    shape, not as literal members of this category.
  * BrakeApplied / EmergencyLanesOn / AirbagDeployed / CrashState /
    ServiceModePlus / Wiper* are NOT present in the generated
    pm.Signals slice for this proto vintage. The wiring text in
    the prompt is aspirational; this prompt's gate (pm.Signals walk)
    only routes fields that actually exist.
  * Wiper* in pm.Signals: WiperHeatEnabled exists but is in the
    climate category and was already routed in prompt 0042.

No classifier ambiguity:
  * pm.Signals shows ZERO safety_security fields that overlap any
    prior routed category. The routing.yaml loader's
    duplicate-field validator (TestLoaderRejectsDuplicateField)
    provides structural enforcement; no duplicates were introduced
    by this prompt.


